WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience cheering)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:03.140
- All hour, we've celebrated
just how valuable friends

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:04.330
are to our happiness.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.620
So let's close out with
one last feel-good story

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:07.453
about friendship.

00:00:07.453 --> 00:00:08.931
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:08.931 --> 00:00:11.760
(upbeat theme music)

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.100
Sometimes you make a friend

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.320
without exactly realizing it at the time.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.950
That's what happened to an
Indiana man named Canyon,

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.650
when he discovered he
had a mouse in his house.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.340
Here he is explaining it on TikTok.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.560
- So there's a mouse in my house
and I can't kill the mouse.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.110
So I got one of these
little like humane catchers

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.960
where you can then like
let them back outside,

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.420
like away from your home.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.600
Okay, so I just came home
from my lunch at work

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.490
and I caught one.

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:35.520
But the problem is,

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:36.620
is that I can't like just drop,

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.000
it's freezing outside right now.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.740
So instead I gave him his own little,

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.130
like this huge cooking pot.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.880
And then inside of it,
please don't jump out.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.580
I gave him like, he's gonna jump out.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:49.550
I gave him like a banana and paper towels.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:52.960
And in case he wants to like
live in there for a minute.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.995
Do I have a pet mouse now?

00:00:54.995 --> 00:00:57.014
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:00:57.014 --> 00:00:59.090
- I think they might need air.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:01.900
Of course, the story of
this budding friendship

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:02.780
didn't end there.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.470
So let's get Canyon on the line right now

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:05.850
to tell us if he gave the mouse air.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:09.045
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:01:09.045 --> 00:01:10.000
So what's up?

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.580
So you really, look, first
of all, we are the same.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:13.540
I cannot kill things.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.950
Like I do not wanna kill something.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:15.960
I try and take it outside.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.390
My friends laugh at me,
but you did, however,

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:21.977
put a lid on something and
maybe there was no air.

00:01:21.977 --> 00:01:22.960
- Yeah.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:23.793
- Yeah.

00:01:23.793 --> 00:01:24.626
- The big concern was
that there was no air

00:01:24.626 --> 00:01:26.410
although it's a very light lid

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.790
and that mouse could have easily
jumped out if it wanted to.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:30.620
So I was thankful that
it did not jump out.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.670
Everyone was concerned
with how much air it had,

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.350
but I was, I couldn't help but look at it.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:35.620
I was constantly lifting the lid.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:37.227
He was, he did a great job.

00:01:37.227 --> 00:01:38.530
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:39.690
- My God, I love you.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:42.010
So Canyon posted the video
of him releasing Julian

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:42.843
back into the wild.

00:01:42.843 --> 00:01:44.336
So let's see it.

00:01:44.336 --> 00:01:46.490
- Okay. This is where
you go live your life.

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:47.410
Oh, hi little guy.

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:49.353
Go on, go live free.

00:01:49.353 --> 00:01:51.110
Wait here, wait.

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:53.320
He's running.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.570
He's so cute.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:55.403
Here.

00:01:55.403 --> 00:01:57.580
If you want, there's snacks,

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:58.760
there's snacks and stuff in here.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.040
I left snacks.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.050
There's snacks, there's a banana.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:06.009
I love you, have a
blessed and fruitful life.

00:02:06.009 --> 00:02:08.446
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:02:08.446 --> 00:02:11.030
- So, how do you think
the mouse is doing now?

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.320
Have you seen the mouse?

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.710
- I, you know, I have gone
and checked on him many times

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:17.440
but I think he's out living his best life.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.120
He's either a bachelor or
he's got kids to take care of

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.610
but I have visited him plenty of times

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:22.540
and he has not been home.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:24.030
So the house is still there

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:26.340
but I think he's just out, you
know, he's out on the town.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:29.140
I mean, I left him more than
any mouse could ever want

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:29.973
so I'm sure he's just

00:02:29.973 --> 00:02:30.806
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:30.806 --> 00:02:32.150
living his best life for sure.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:33.798
- Oh my God, I love you Canyon.

00:02:33.798 --> 00:02:34.631
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:02:34.631 --> 00:02:36.638
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:36.638 --> 00:02:37.471
(message tone dings)

00:02:37.471 --> 00:02:38.304
That's not all though.

00:02:38.304 --> 00:02:40.080
Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:42.670
makers of G2, the go-to pen
of the Kelly Clarkson show,

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:45.590
wanna honor ultimate
over-achievers, just like you, sir.

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:47.790
So they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:48.969
to help out other mice.

00:02:48.969 --> 00:02:52.318
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:02:52.318 --> 00:02:53.665
- Thank you so much, thank you.

00:02:53.665 --> 00:02:54.659
- Thank you so much.

00:02:54.659 --> 00:02:58.683
- That's wonderful.
(audience cheering)

